       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions)\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day, typical for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg per day**, divided into a different schedule\n\nIf you want the dose as written, please confirm it and give the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, but I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
